### A dispatcher is no instance operator: running a schedule is a Management API `developer` operation, which the
### descriptor's `access.developer` grants to the `admin` role only
# @name DispatcherRunsNow
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
POST {{fshBaseUrl}}/management/projects/field-service/schedules/overdue-report/run
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The administrator's *Run now* (spec ruling R8): the host's cron stays `0 6 * * *`, and the suite starts one run
### outside it, one per tenant the host's catalog lists — no test switch in the host. 200 with the run it started.
# @name AdminRunsNow
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fshBaseUrl}}/management/projects/field-service/schedules/overdue-report/run
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyAdmin}}

### What the dispatch desks received — polled until both tenants' reports are in, at most ~30 s
# @name OverdueReports
## RETRY-UNTIL-TEST-PASS: Both tenants received their overdue report.
## RETRY-MAX-ATTEMPTS: 30
## RETRY-BACKOFF-TYPE: Constant
## RETRY-MAX-DELAY: 00:00:01
POST {{fshSinkUrl}}/__admin/requests/find
Content-Type: application/json

{ "method": "POST", "urlPath": "/notifications/reports/overdue" }
